<section
  class="section wrap approach-section"
  id="approach"
  aria-labelledby="approach-heading"
  data-discovery-section="approach"
>
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 / How I work</p>
    <h2 id="approach-heading">
      <span>How I work.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="principles">
    <article class="principle">
      <h3>Setting technical direction</h3>
      <p>
        I evaluate options, explain trade-offs and shape architecture that other
        developers can build on. When modernising existing systems, I balance
        technical debt, dependencies and migration risk with the needs of a live
        product.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <h3>Turning requirements into delivery</h3>
      <p>
        I work with product, design and backend teams to clarify requirements,
        challenge assumptions and agree a practical approach. I break ambiguous
        work into deliverable steps, set priorities and connect UX and design
        decisions with the engineering needed to deliver them.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <h3>Helping the team build better</h3>
      <p>
        I mentor developers, review code and improve shared components, testing
        and tooling. I use AI extensively in my development workflow and build
        AI-assisted automations that help the team tackle recurring tasks.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <h3>Owning what reaches production</h3>
      <p>
        My responsibility continues after release. I work on build and
        deployment infrastructure, monitor errors, investigate incidents and
        diagnose performance problems, using what I learn in production to guide
        further improvements.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <h3>Building for the people using it</h3>
      <p>
        I make accessibility, internationalisation, mobile optimisation and
        performance part of product and architecture decisions from the start. I
        balance usability, security and privacy with the constraints of the
        platform, so the experience works well for the people relying on it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

